      "spoken": {
        "role": "intro",
        "said": "This is an open question, not an explainer. Two repositories, one person, and a crowd of agent sessions all merge into GitHub on a free personal account, and the merges wait in line. I'll show where the time goes, with the numbers, what we settled on, and why we still don't like it. If you know a better pattern that stays on GitHub and costs nothing, that's the part I'm asking for. It's as of November twenty-third, twenty twenty-six."
      },
      "durationMs": 31900
    },
    {
