            "title": "Settle every branch, then land them together",
            "steps": [
              {
                "badge": "main",
                "label": "Settle",
                "note": "Review, fixes and local checks, before any PR"
              },
              {
                "badge": "main",
                "label": "Bucket",
                "note": "One to seven settled branches in one PR"
              },
              {
                "badge": "main",
                "label": "One CI round",
                "note": "Instead of one per branch, per merge"
              },
              {
                "badge": "main",
                "label": "Fix the filter",
                "note": "CD1 (#3388) and #3394, landed"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "spoken": {
        "role": "scene",
        "chapter": "Chapter three. What we chose.",
        "narration": "What we settled on has two parts. First, a branch does all its settling before it ever opens a pull request: review, fixes, and the checks a laptop can run. Then one to seven settled branches land together in one bucket, so one CI round covers all of them. Second, fix the filter, so a change only runs the jobs it can fail."
      },
      "durationMs": 27700
    },
    {
      "id": "H1",
      "picture": {
        "kind": "card"
      },
      "burnIns": [
        {
          "kind": "cheat-sheet",
          "params": {
            "kicker": "STILL HURTS",
            "title": "What buckets don't fix",
            "rows": [
              {
                "task": "A red bucket",
                "command": "1-7 branches wait",
                "note": "one flaky test holds back every branch in it",
                "badge": "gap"
              },
              {
                "task": "A revert",
                "command": "pick it out of a bucket",
                "note": "is coarser: it lands with its bucket",
                "badge": "gap"
              },
              {
                "task": "Pairs",
                "command": "some-ui, then server",
                "note": "a ledger or fixture lands here first, then the server re-runs",
                "badge": "gap"
              },
              {
                "task": "One pool",
                "command": "both repos, one queue",
                "note": "both repos share the runners; the queue never clears",
                "badge": "gap"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "spoken": {
        "role": "scene",
        "chapter": "Chapter four. What still hurts.",
        "narration": "Buckets trade one pain for others. A single flaky test now holds back several branches, not one. Reverting a feature means picking it back out of a bucket. Changes that come in pairs across the two repositories still go one after the other. And both repositories share one pool of runners, so under load the queue never clears."
      },
      "durationMs": 25700
    },
