      "spoken": {
        "role": "scene",
        "chapter": "Chapter five. The open question.",
        "narration": "Here's where I'd like help. A free organization seems to get the merge queue on public repositories, so moving there might be the whole answer, if nothing else breaks. Or a train: a bot branch that tests a batch once and then fast-forwards main. Or a looser gate on the pull request, the full suite on main, and a revert when it goes red. Each one gives something up. Which would you pick, or what are we missing?"
      },
      "durationMs": 33400
    },
